like the way you spoon it to me  [Laughter]  hi welcome back to chasing our roots i'm  vanessa and today we're hanging out with  chef erica lacer from diva dog so we're  going to be doing our apple pie bread  pudding and i use a liquor that has like  apple flavoring to it for the sauce i've  had that before not have that  combination okay well good i would say  that it's an easy dish but it depends on  the type of cook you are so i am really  excited to make this dessert with you so  let's go ahead and get into it we have  five eggs here right how to mix that up  a little bit so we're gonna put the milk  but i'm not gonna put all the milk i'm  kind of reserved a little bit so we have  the cream here that we're gonna add in  so my storefront i loved it was like all  brick on the inside but it was like i  was there every day couldn't get away  that's not what i wanted to do i wanted  to have a business where i had the  freedom to still be creative so has your  menu or recipes changed because you're  not using a storefront anymore you're on  a food truck so i had to condense my  menu a little bit so i just cut it down  to two which is my diva dog and the  alligator sausage as well as just some  other items that i have of course the  bread pudding we're gonna put a little  bit of sugar and i always put more sugar  than i probably need and then we have  our vanilla cinnamon and then we just  mix all of this together to make our  custard i'm the kind of cook that  doesn't really measure so i'm i'm going  to try to go buy a recipe i just know  it's going to come out the way i like it  i put love into my food and when i'm in  a great mood my food tastes even better  go as close as you can without taking  off too much of the apple just take it  cut the sides off and i'm a girl that  hates to waste anything i take  everything off so why do you choose to  use granny smith apples instead of like  a red delicious apple gritty sweet is  pretty much a traditional apple that you  use if you made apple pie apple pie and  bread pudding like typically aren't  supposed to go together but you have  that custardy style flavor soaked in  with this baked gummy bread so let's add  in the bread this is nice and moist  right here and so now we can add in our  apples that we cut okay and i like that  it's like the chunks are not too big so  this definitely smells like the  beginning of fall like the seasons  changing i mean it works year-round for  my customers i use my hot dog buns like  it was a moment where i had ordered too  many buns for an event i can't throw  this bread away like i just cannot do it  and so i grind it all up and kind of  made bread pudding and it tastes better  than when i was using french bread and  this is kind of like a technique i  learned when i was in culinary school so  we're going to pour that in there i make  it the same way i was taught as a little  girl and make it now we're going to put  in the oven at 350. so when i'm at home  it's just pretty much putting cream in a  pot thicken it up with some cornstarch  adding sugar to it and as much liquor as  you want to and drizzle that right on  top um i put on the stove brought it to  a bowl and it kind of reduced a little  bit so we'll add like a little bit of  corn starch to it so this is just going  to thicken it up just a little bit more  so it'll be more pudding-like and put a  little bit more cinnamon sugar and we're  going to taste this here and for me i  still need more sugar  and so now we're ready for the good part  that  nice apple smells  definitely going to help everything come  together this is going to be so good so  it's nice and good so we put that back  on the sofa a little bit i'm chefing it  up you can really see that it's like  really thickening up yeah nice thickness  to where it just comes off really really  smooth on your spoon spatula whatever  you're using this is gonna be good to go  right here i like this consistency right  here so we're going to put that in the  bowl and watch how pudding like it comes  out so we'll just add a little bit of  the apples here sauce is nice and ready  for us so let's go get the pudding okay  all right see that color nice and golden  it's like really crunchy is it you can  tell because it starts to kind of puff  up just like a little bit so i just kind  of take a butter knife and kind of dab  it in the middle just to make sure that  center is kind of cooking all the way  through what i want to do just to make  it pretty for presentation wise now i do  not do this on the truck pop that on the  plate look how beautiful that is wow you  can see like a definitive crust and then  like the gooeyness of the bread pudding  just take that sauce and you put it on  it however you want i think we still  have some cut apples over here  i present to you my cognac apple pie  bread pudding thank you so much chef  erica i am so excited to try this i'm  going to dig into this right now please  enjoy it  so we're going to go ahead and dive in  food perfect you can change the crunches  of the apples the crispy layer all the  moisture inside the bread pudding  cinnamon and the sugar it all comes  together and even that like hints of  cognac you can taste all of that passion  that she really puts into her food is so  so good yeah try it  it's funny because i don't like apple  pie but i like this  really good you guys have to just come  to new orleans and just try this for  yourself check out the bread pudding it  is so amazing here so that's it for us  here at diva dog thank you to chef erica  and her entire team for letting us come  hang out and thank you for watching  tasting our roots bye  [Music]  you

